# Git stores text with LF and hands it back the same way, on every machine.
# Without this, Windows checks out CRLF, Prettier expects LF, and `format:check`
# fails locally on files nobody has touched while CI stays green on Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Left byte for byte. `text=auto` would guess right on most of these, but a CV
# is not the place to find out.
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.webp binary
